        "digitized_from": "Real OpenStreetMap building footprints for both towers (OSM ways 1410182008 '1655 3rd St / Uber Headquarters Building 3' and 1410183655 '1725 3rd St / Uber Headquarters Building 4'), unioned into one MultiPolygon.",
        "digitization_method": "ADDED (as status.csv row, blklot 8722063): two 11-story, LEED Gold office towers developed by a joint venture of Alexandria Real Estate Equities, Uber Technologies and the Golden State Warriors, designed by SHoP Architects, completed 2021. Grouped as one record since the two towers' airspace-condo office units (blklots 8722063 for 1655 3rd and 8722087 for 1725 3rd) share one identical underlying land parcel polygon in DataSF's own parcel map. MIGRATED 2026-09-23 from status.csv to this hand geometry, per the owner's direct instruction: that shared underlying parcel is the WHOLE Blocks 29-32 superblock -- the same polygon also used for Chase Center (blklot 8722025), making the two towers visually indistinguishable from the arena on the map. Replaced the shared-parcel join with the two towers' own real, individually-surveyed OpenStreetMap building footprints, unioned into one MultiPolygon (they are two separate, non-touching buildings, ~8,732 sqm combined) -- see mission_bay_chase_center.geojson's own digitization_method for the corresponding Chase Center fix. 2026-09-29 accuracy audit: none of the pages cited for 'designed by SHoP Architects' names SHoP. ArchDaily's 'Uber Headquarters / SHoP Architects' page credits SHoP but lists 423,000 ft2 and 2022, so it may not cover exactly these two towers; Office Snapshots credits the interiors of Buildings 3 and 4 to Huntsman Architectural Group. Both are now cited.",
        "accuracy_caveat": "REAL -- each tower's footprint is an individually surveyed OpenStreetMap building outline (not a hand trace, not the shared Assessor parcel), cross-checked visually against Esri satellite imagery.",
        "notes": "1725 3rd St directly adjoins Chase Center. Uber's SEC EDGAR company record lists 1725 3rd Street as its business address (read 2026-09-29), though a May 2023 SF Standard report said that specific building had never been occupied by Uber and was being marketed for sublease (an Uber spokesperson: 'currently unoccupied') -- current occupancy is genuinely unclear and not resolved here.",
